{
  "description": "U8 damage tracking in the compositor (#220): CPU per shown frame, shown frames per second, CPU per second and memory with frames without a change skipped (Skip, the default), with only the damage composited into a target per view (Target, BL_DAMAGE=target) and with every frame composited and shown (Off, BL_DAMAGE=0), all on the same engine (site 0, main with U8; all three count only frames with a change), and the engine before U8 (E0, site 1, counts every frame) for the correction check. Pages: CSS animation, 360p video, WebGL and scrolling (every frame changes the whole view, so Target composites straight into the framebuffer there and may cost at most 3 % more), plus idle (an animation outside the view, nothing visible changes: only CPU per second, frames.mjs reports no frame rate there). Rule R under SwiftShader (owner decision): the lever is CPU per second on idle, the other pages may not get worse (rule correction). engine_runs: <U8 run>,<run before U8>",
  "metrics": [
    "cpuPerFrame",
    "fps",
    "cpuPerSecond"
  ],
  "secondary": [],
  "configs": [
    {
      "name": "Skip",
      "site": 0
    },
    {
      "name": "Target",
      "site": 0,
      "engine": {
        "env": {
          "BL_DAMAGE": "target"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Off",
      "site": 0,
      "engine": {
        "env": {
          "BL_DAMAGE": "0"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "E0",
      "site": 1
    }
  ],
  "compare": [
    {
      "base": "Off",
      "arms": [
        "Skip",
        "Target"
      ],
      "rule": "lever",
      "where": {
        "site": "idle"
      }
    },
    {
      "base": "Off",
      "arms": [
        "Skip",
        "Target"
      ],
      "rule": "correction"
    },
    {
      "base": "E0",
      "arms": [
        "Skip",
        "Target",
        "Off"
      ],
      "rule": "correction"
    }
  ],
  "groups": [
